        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">If you have the floor space, buy a dual-stack functional trainer
            such as the REP Arcadia</strong>; if you already own a compatible REP rack, the Athena
            puts the same stack inside it; and if money is tight and you own plates, the Bells of
            Steel Cable Tower gets you a proper adjustable cable for the least. Choose a digital
            machine for guided training and a clear floor, not for maximum load.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever type you choose, halve a 2:1 stack to know what it really feels like, measure
            the ceiling at the exact spot, and anchor the frame exactly as its maker specifies. If
